turn-blend
An all-in-one voice activity and end-of-turn detection model.

turn-blend.onnx (version 0.2.0) is one ONNX graph made of the parts below. The third-party graphs were
converted to ONNX opset 18 where needed, renamed with a per-model prefix and joined into one graph.

1. Silero VAD v6.2 (unmodified weights)
   Copyright (c) 2020-present Silero Team. MIT License (licenses/silero-vad-MIT.txt).
   https://github.com/snakers4/silero-vad
   The published 16 kHz graph was specialised to a fixed input shape with its control flow folded away.

2. turn-1-mini by p99lab (unmodified weights)
   Copyright 2026 p99lab. Apache License, Version 2.0 (licenses/turn-1-mini-Apache-2.0.txt).
   https://huggingface.co/p99lab/turn-1-mini
   Its NOTICE file is reproduced in full below, as section 4(d) of the Apache License requires.
   Changes made to the turn-1-mini ONNX graph (onnx/turn-1-mini.step.onnx): opset 17 to 18, tensor names
   prefixed with "mini/", embedded in a larger graph. Weights unchanged.

3. The student model (new in 0.2.0; weights trained for turn-blend)
   An OpenAI Whisper Base encoder with a small pooling head, fine-tuned to reproduce the end-of-turn scores
   of turn-1 by p99lab.
   - Encoder initialised from Whisper Base. Copyright (c) 2022 OpenAI. MIT License (licenses/whisper-MIT.txt).
     https://github.com/openai/whisper   https://huggingface.co/openai/whisper-base
   - Training targets: scores produced by turn-1 by p99lab. Copyright 2026 p99lab. Apache License, Version 2.0
     (same text as licenses/turn-1-mini-Apache-2.0.txt). https://huggingface.co/p99lab/turn-1
     No turn-1 weights are inside turn-blend.onnx. Because the student was trained on turn-1's outputs, the
     turn-1 NOTICE file is kept with this model (licenses/turn-1-NOTICE.txt) and reproduced below.
   - Training audio (processed for training, not redistributed here), all CC BY 4.0
     (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/); their authors do not endorse turn-blend:
       HarperValleyBank. C. Wu, M. Nafziger, A. Scodary, A. Maas, "HarperValleyBank: A Domain-Specific Spoken
         Dialog Corpus", arXiv:2010.13929. https://github.com/cricketclub/gridspace-stanford-harper-valley
       AMI Meeting Corpus. J. Carletta et al., "The AMI Meeting Corpus: A Pre-announcement", MLMI 2005.
         https://groups.inf.ed.ac.uk/ami/corpus/
       Smart Turn training data v3.2 (English part), Pipecat / Daily.
         https://huggingface.co/datasets/pipecat-ai/smart-turn-data-v3.2-train

Versions up to 0.1.0 contained Smart Turn v3.2 (Copyright (c) 2024-2025, Daily, BSD 2-Clause). Version 0.2.0
does not contain Smart Turn weights.

The blend weights in this model were fitted on held-out windows of HarperValleyBank and AMI. The default
commit threshold was chosen with LiveKit's eot-bench data in view. The model is evaluated on that data
(https://huggingface.co/datasets/livekit/eot-bench-data, CC BY 4.0 per its dataset card;
harness https://github.com/livekit/eot-bench, Apache-2.0); it was not trained on it and its blend weights
were not fitted on it.

turn-blend is not affiliated with or endorsed by Silero, Daily, Pipecat, p99lab, OpenAI or LiveKit. The names
of the component models are used only to identify them.

